{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "What a panel response pushes against (walls) or leans toward (pulls), as data. Loaded by app/services/objections.py. Keyed to a person's SITUATION, never a sector: 'costs something just to reach it' is a no-car, far-from-town objection whether the pitch is a clinic, a bank or a school. Fieldwork-collected types slot in here as new rows; no code change. Cues are scored against the stored answer archive (scripts/shadow_objections.py): a cue that NEVER fires on a real instance of its wall is noise and comes out. A cue that is merely wrong more often than right stays — it is still the only way this layer can see a true case, and that trade needs a reader, not a shorter list.",
