        }
      ],
      "definition": {
        "what": "They want a real person to help them when something goes wrong, and doubt one will be there. A branch, a counter, staff, someone accountable who can fix a mistake.",
        "not_for": "Merely mentioning a person. Consulting a spouse, a parent or the group before deciding is a household decision, not a complaint about support. Asking for a demonstration is a learning need, not a support gap.",
        "examples": [
          "If the money goes missing, who do I walk in and see?",
          "There is no office here. You phone and phone and nobody answers."
        ]
      }
    },
